      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Currie earned the nickname \"Gateway to Lake Shetek,\" the largest lake in southwestern Minnesota, and hosts the End‑O‑Line Railroad Park and Museum.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Currie%2C_Minnesota",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Des Moines River originates just north of Currie, flowing from Lake Shetek and passing through the town's northern side.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Currie%2C_Minnesota",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The original Currie store building, now housed in End‑O‑Line Park, stands as a tangible reminder of the town's early commercial roots.",
